# Colours for treepine.obj.
#
# Every channel is a multiple of 0x11, because the panel is four bits per
# channel and a colour that is not shifts on the device and nowhere else.
# Each Kd is a sixteenth, so obj2cpp's round(v * 255) lands back exactly on
# the byte it was written for.
#
# The same greens pine.obj and the tree sprites use. A tree in the middle of
# a route, a tree on its border and a tree behind a battle are all one
# forest, and that only holds if the colours are literally the same numbers.

newmtl pine_needles
Kd 0.333333 0.666667 0.333333   # #55AA55

newmtl pine_bark
Kd 0.466667 0.333333 0.200000   # #775533
